<title>BELGIUM: Belgium forecasts falling deficit/GDP.</title>
<headline>Belgium forecasts falling deficit/GDP.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-10-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Belgian government said in a statement on the 1997 budget on Tuesday that, based on the budget, it forecast a ratio of the budget deficit to gross domestic product of 2.5 percent in 1998.</p>
<p>Based on the budget a simulation applying the budget data to the medium-term forecasts by the planning bureau allowed for the following forecasts for the deficit/GDP ratio to be made as well - two percent in 1999 and 1.6 percent in the year 2000.</p>
<p>Taking into account the measures in the 1997 budget, the ratio would be at 2.9 percent in 1997.</p>
</text>
